{{GuideIntroClass|Shaman}}

==Introduction==
{{ClassTooltip|class_name = Shaman}} is a fairly simple class that has the greater time scaling of all classes and the best enchantment scaling pre-ascension, by a large margin, only getting beaten by Dread Heretic after ascensions is reached. Its main profits come from idle bonus (main one) and summon efficiency (second in order of importance). 

While the class excels at long runs, it is still viable with shorter exiles early in the realm. It demonstrates its true power after e550 mysts with access to T3 pets and as one of the myst pushing powerhouses during the lategame.

Pros
* Easy to learn and play
* Low AP dependency
* Can burst multiple times with short weapon re-stacking phase
* Best scaling with enchants pre-ascension in the whole game
* Excellent time and enchant scaling

Cons
* Item requirements (ideally all required sets at legendary quality for enchantments)
* Expensive to min-max due to high value per enchant

===Attribute Points===
{{ClassTooltip|class_name = Shaman}} is pretty lucky compared to other classes since the bare minimum points needed are only 815

* Intelligence 150
* Insight 90 (with {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Legacy}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Netherfist}} to reach all VM items requisites)
* Spellcraft 150 (175 if you don't have legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Boots Of Harsh Trials}})
* Patience 200
* Mastery 150 (200 if you don't own legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Rugged Wristcoat}})
* Empathy 0 (75 if you don't own legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name = Bite Sleeves}})

<br />After that try to reach these goals
# Emp 100 (to reach 175 with {{ItemTooltip|item_name = Bite Sleeves}} equipped, so you can use both {{ItemTooltip|item_name = Falconer's Warm Cape}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name = Hollow Eye Pendant}})
# dom 135 (150 if you don't own legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Rugged Wristcoat}})
# emp 200 (dom down to 100)
# dom 185 (200 if you don't own legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Rugged Wristcoat}})

===E550 myst variation===
We assume the following initial AP distribution:

* 150 Intelligence
* 90 Insight (which becomes 150 with legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name = Netherfist}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Legacy}} equipped)
* 175 Spellcraft (to equip gear)
* 0 Wisdom
* 75 Dominance (if there aren't enough points, drop Dominance)
* 200 Patience (which becomes 250 with legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Encircling Trophies}} equipped)
* 100 Mastery
* 175 Empathy (which becomes 250 with legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Bite Sleeves}} equipped)

Now distribute points according to the following priority list (you need to achieve the requested value at a point in order to go to the following):

# 200 Mastery
# 160 Insight (which becomes 250 with the VM set)
# 250 Mastery
# 100 Dominance (which becomes 250 with legendary {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Voidstrike Seal}})
# 250 Intelligence
# Dump: Patience > Empathy > Dominance > Insight > Versatility
# 250 Spellcraft exactly (take points out of Versatility to reach)
# ''Optional'': If Wisdom 150 perk gives more than 1.3e3 profits on your exiles, push your Versatility points into it
# 250 Wisdom exactly (take points out of Versatility to reach)

dumps: pat > mas > emp > dom > int > ins > ver

