Stack {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Conjure Primal Elemental}} for a bit before swapping to {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Summon Centipede Swarm}} to get more clicks.

This phase should last however long your exile is planned on being, minus about 3 days. Then, those final 3 days should be in the following pet time stacking phase. For shorter exiles, spend about 10% of the exile on this phase, then move on to Autoclick Stacking on short exiles, or Pet Time Stacking on long exiles.

''note: The order of spells matters here.''

''note: Early in the realm it might be a good idea to use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Conjure Greater Elemental}} in order to help charge spells (like {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Nightfall}}). Swap out {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Conjure Primal Elemental}}.''

===Pet time stacking===
{{GuideBox|pet=Herald of Rot|pet1=Risen Giant|
spells=#2#PetTimeStack@18,2;21,2;92,2;72,2;59,2;58,2|
itemtab=Items|items=#2#PetTimeStack@115;113;7;23;18;39;44;60;57;88;77;1003;208;302;414;415;90;2001;3007;504|}}

This set is to Boost {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Herald of Rot}} and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Risen Giant}} game time and increase their profits

At around 60 casts per sec of plague zombies you reach HoR's game time soft cap of 200 days after 80 hours of this phase.  RG's softcap of 14 days can be reached in a bit over 5 and a half hours, however, RG's time scaling is weaker and generally not done for long periods of time.

If you play shorter exiles, spend up to 1-2 minutes on this phase with RG after the VM phase, then level the pet a bit before bursting. This should give you more profit than just moving onto burst out of the VM phase.

===<span style="color:yellow">Optional Phase: Autoclick Stacking</span>===
{{GuideBox|pet=Ley Keeper|
spells=#3#AClickStack@26,2;25,2;18,2;92,2;16,2;104,2|
itemtab=Autoclick Stacking|items=#3#AClickStack@115;113;7;23;18;31;44;60;57;88;74;1023;212;302;415;406;97;2003;3007;504}}

As detailed in the Voidmana phase, it is worth spending most of your time during shorter exiles stacking autoclicks, which is done during this phase. This is because you only stack Pet time for a few minutes after gathering VM, and as mentioned before, stacking spells isn't worth on short exiles to begin with. Items used solely in this phase aren't enchanted, as their enchants don't provide any value. 
===Branch Charging===
The goal here is to stack up charges (through autoclicks) on {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Branch of the Great Cycle}}. Because {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Summon Centipede Swarm}} scales the number of autoclicks on Summon efficiency, we maximize that (and, when we can't, we do CAP because CAP^.155 = Summon eff).

{{GuideBox|pet=Herald of Rot|pet1=Ley Keeper|
spells=#4#Branch@18,2;92,2;26,2;23,2;25,2;70,2|
itemtab=Items|items=#4#Branch@115;113;7;23;18;31;44;60;57;88;74;1001;208;302;418;406;97;2009;3007;504|
note=If you don't have the second trophy swap it out with {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Intact Carapace}}.}}

Note: if you have the Ingot Shortage Triumph you can try to see if {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Recaller Stone}} in the offhand, {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Seclusion Shell}} in the body slot and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Concealing Shroud}} in the back slot are worth more total clicks compared to the suggested items and change accordingly as character levels should be worth more than summon efficiency in this phase thanks to {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Eerie Turquoise Phylactery}}. {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Ley Keeper}} can make this phase much faster on shorter exiles.

===Void Mana===
There's two ways to go about VM gathering, depending on the length of your exile: 

Option 1: We use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Void Radiance}} to gather VM on longer exiles since we don't want to lose all that stacked time on our burst pet, so all the items we use gives more VM per entity or incantation efficiency.

Option 2: We use {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Voidterror|display_name=Voidterror}} to gather VM, and then follow that up by stacking pet time on our burst pet of choice immediately after, for about 2 minutes. This is generally superior when you're early into the realm, and it works great for faster exiles. However, this will eventually be outclassed on longer exiles purely from the time scaling of {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Herald of Rot}} and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Risen Giant}}. If you decide to go with this method for faster exiles, spend some time stacking autoclicks with the optional Autoclick Stacking phase that was mentioned before. 

