==Refinement==
===Item Stats Priority===
There are a few things that impact on your total profit. This is what to prioritize before you have fully upgraded all the items suggested by the guide, so you can make an educated decision on what to swap. Remember that set bonuses usually take priority over other non-upgraded items.

*Idle Bonus > Summoning Efficiency = Character Ability Power(CAP) > Pet Ability Power(PAP) > Click/ Autoclick Profit > Profit

*Idle Bonus is the strongest stat you can ever get with shaman as everything you do scales it (Patience, CAP, PAP, Summon Eff).

*Summoning Efficiency is the second strongest stat for burst as you have 5 summons on the bar, giving it a x5 relevance, '''BUT''' CAP scales both Idle Bonus and Summon Eff so it's above it in the scale of things.

*While {{PetTooltip|Herald of Rot}} PAP scaling is kinda low, it has 3 relevant profit abilities and one of them is Summon Eff. With {{PetTooltip|Risen Giant}} swap the priority of PAP and Click Profit as PAP has a lower value, apart from a few cases where you get a ton of it (like {{ItemTooltip|Bite Sleeves}}).

*Finally you have Click/Autoclick Profit and Profit, the first getting prioritised as usually the items with it have other more useful stats for the class, ideally you only want to see {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Resonator Ring}} with these stats, but {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Embrace Of The Grove}} is better than {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Falconer's Warm Cape}} with {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Risen Giant}} before ench where {{ItemTooltip|item_name=The Magnifier}} take priority.

===Resource Spending===
Here are some tips on how to spend your dust to upgrade and improve your gear as a new Shaman.

* Get {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Branch of the Great Cycle}} > {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Cold-blooded Ring}} > {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Resonator Ring}} to '''legendary'''. Branch and cbr have the biggest priority. {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Heart of the Grave}} is useful to upgrade if you plan to go offline during pet time stacking.
* Farm Shattered Reality, Eye of Chaos and Cathedral in expedition to get and upgrade {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Charged Fin-Wing}}, {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Insidious Lure}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Warbanner Fragment}} to '''legendary'''. Spend unstable keys on lower level zones first as they're cheaper.
* Useful legendary items: {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Perfected Kata Bracers}}, {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Frosty Ring}} and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Artificer's Shoulderpads}}, they're a real boon to longer runs.
* Get a few enchants on {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Temporal Scabbard}} to help out with the stacking.
* Burst items have the upgrade priority, followed by vm gen and branch stacking after you have your legendary weapons.

