==Ascension (T3) classes==
After you reach e1100 Mysteries Shaman have access to two [[Ascension_Forms|Ascension Forms]] they can pick from: [[Demiurge]] and [[Defiance]].

===Demiurge===
[[Demiurge]] gives access to an additional mana source with a very powerful unique memetic and catalysts based on the highest number of catalysts you have on a source, reduced mana cost for sources based on ascension level and access to 3 more spells: {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Primal Power}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Conjure Void Elemental}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Forge Empyreal Vassal}}. While the first is mostly useless due to the nature of shaman, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Conjure Void Elemental}} is incredibly powerful thanks to the incredible amount of summon efficiency shaman can get and the fact that it can be pre-buffed by {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Voidterror}} before switching to {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Herald of Rot}} instead of relying on just {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Void Lure}} + {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Void Radiance}}. Finally {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Forge Empyreal Vassal}} is a permanent incantation (the bonuses last until exile and  the spell itself does not need to be on the spellbar for them to be applied) that increase your pet ability power, mostly for {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Voidterror}} and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Herald of Rot}}.

The full guide can be found here: [[Demiurge Shaman Guide]]

===Defiance===
[[Defiance]] has a '''Transcendant''' form that provides different bonuses depending on if it is charging or activated. While charging, it increases your void mana per entity by a huge amount. Once activated, it increases your click profit and your summoning efficiency instead (if you want to use it with other classes don't worry, this bonus changes based on the T2 you're playing as). It also gives you access to 3 more spells: {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Unclean Knowledge}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Nullzone}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Employ Celestial Countermeasures}}. While {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Nullzone}} suffers from the same fate as {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Primal Power}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Unclean Knowledge}} partially changes the way {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Herald of Rot}} is leveled while also slightly increasing shaman's time and enchant scaling, finally {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Employ Celestial Countermeasures}} is another permanent incantation, this time increasing evocation and summoning efficiency. While the first part is only nice for {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Synthetic Entity}} the second part is shaman's bread and butter.

The full guide can be found here: [[Defiance Shaman Guide]]